<newsitem itemid="115384" id="root" date="1996-10-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Highland 1996 pre-tax profit falls.</title>
<headline>Highland 1996 pre-tax profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Aug 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence, diluted)   20.1		   vs 21.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.3		    vs 6.0</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 8.3		    vs 7.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     37.1		   vs 42.9</p>
<p> Turnover		   184.8		  vs 180.6</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 39.2 to 42.5 million stg.</p>
<p> Operating result	 36.5		    vs 36.5</p>
<p> Exceptional cost	 3.0		     vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		   3.6		     vs 6.4</p>
<p> Tax			  9.9		     vs 14.0</p>
<p> Minorities		 0.3		     vs 0.1 loss</p>
<p> Attributable	     27.5		    vs 28.8</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 9, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  December 10, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Whisky producer Highland Distilleries said that the exceptional charge related to reorganisation costs and the cost of its successful bid for Macallan-Glenlivet whisky.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
